---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/pages/the-operator.css';
---

<Layout title="The Operator: Christopher Campbell" description="Technology, construction, and insurance formed the operating discipline behind SecureProspective.">
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" class="operator-page" transition:name="page-card">
    <section class="operator-hero" aria-labelledby="operator-title">
      <div class="operator-hero-grid shell">
        <aside class="operator-hero-rail" aria-label="Operator file">
          <div class="operator-rail-top">
            <span>FILE // OPERATOR</span>
            <span>STATE // ACTIVE</span>
          </div>
          <div class="operator-rail-mark" aria-hidden="true">
            <span>03</span>
            <i></i>
          </div>
          <div class="operator-rail-bottom">
            <span>C. CAMPBELL</span>
            <span>INSIDE THE WORK</span>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="operator-hero-main">
          <div class="operator-hero-copy">
            <h1 id="operator-title">Built inside<br /><span>the work.</span></h1>
            <p>
              Christopher Campbell did not leave operating responsibility behind to become a consultant.
              SecureProspective is being built from inside the business he still has to run.
            </p>
            <a class="operator-hero-link" href="#operator-careers">Trace the operating spine <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          </div>

          <aside class="operator-hero-condition">
            <span>OPERATING RESPONSIBILITY</span>
            <strong>Still in the room.</strong>
            <p>Technology, construction, and insurance do not sit behind the method. They feed it.</p>
          </aside>

          <ol class="operator-route" aria-label="Three careers feeding the operating method">
            <li class="is-current" data-route-key="technology">
              <span class="operator-route-index">01</span>
              <strong>Technology</strong>
              <small>Passion / Transform</small>
            </li>
            <li data-route-key="construction">
              <span class="operator-route-index">02</span>
              <strong>Construction</strong>
              <small>Objective truth / Diagnose</small>
            </li>
            <li data-route-key="insurance">
              <span class="operator-route-index">03</span>
              <strong>Insurance</strong>
              <small>Responsibility / Position + Shape</small>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="operator-thesis" aria-labelledby="operator-thesis-title">
      <div class="operator-thesis-grid shell">
        <div class="operator-thesis-index">
          <span>THE SPINE</span>
          <span>THREE CAREERS</span>
        </div>
        <div class="operator-thesis-copy">
          <h2 id="operator-thesis-title">Three careers feed the method.</h2>
          <p class="operator-thesis-statement">
            Technology looks ahead. Construction refuses a false reading. Insurance protects the person who lives with the outcome.
          </p>
          <p class="operator-thesis-close">SecureProspective joins all three inside one operating business.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="operator-careers" class="operator-career-record" aria-labelledby="operator-careers-title">
      <div class="operator-record-head shell">
        <div class="operator-record-index">
          <span>FIELD RECORD</span>
          <span>CONTRIBUTIONS // 03</span>
        </div>
        <div class="operator-record-intro">
          <h2 id="operator-careers-title">What each career contributes.</h2>
          <p>The mapping is the point. Each career supplied a different test for work that has to hold up under consequence.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="operator-map shell" data-inspection-map>
        <div class="operator-map-spine" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>

        <article class="operator-station operator-station--technology" data-station="technology">
          <div class="operator-station-index">01</div>
          <div class="operator-station-core">
            <div class="operator-station-heading">
              <span>TECHNOLOGY</span>
              <h3>The passion.</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Technology taught Christopher to see the future state before it arrives and build toward it.
              He started at MCI WorldCom in 1999 at age nineteen, then worked field deployments for Bank of America,
              the USDA wide-area network, and Cisco infrastructure. Twenty-six years in technology make the prospective
              half of the name practical, not fashionable.
            </p>
            <dl class="operator-facts">
              <div><dt>Started</dt><dd>MCI WorldCom, 1999</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Field environments</dt><dd>Bank of America, USDA WAN, Cisco infrastructure</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
          <div class="operator-station-transfer">
            <span>METHOD CONTRIBUTION</span>
            <strong>Transform</strong>
            <p>See the future state before it arrives. Build toward it.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="operator-station operator-station--construction" data-station="construction">
          <div class="operator-station-index">02</div>
          <div class="operator-station-core">
            <div class="operator-station-heading">
              <span>CONSTRUCTION</span>
              <h3>The objective truth.</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Fifteen years of electrical work across commercial, residential, and military environments.
              Voltage is present or it is not. Code is right or it is wrong. There is no persuasive language
              that repairs a false reading. That discipline became Diagnose.
            </p>
            <dl class="operator-facts">
              <div><dt>Duration</dt><dd>Fifteen years</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Work</dt><dd>Commercial, residential, military bases, low voltage, fire alarm</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
          <div class="operator-station-transfer">
            <span>METHOD CONTRIBUTION</span>
            <strong>Diagnose</strong>
            <p>Read what is present before a solution is allowed to speak.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="operator-station operator-station--insurance" data-station="insurance">
          <div class="operator-station-index">03</div>
          <div class="operator-station-core">
            <div class="operator-station-heading">
              <span>INSURANCE</span>
              <h3>The responsibility.</h3>
            </div>
            <p>
              Life insurance, annuity, producer development, and running an IMO put long-range outcomes in the
              work. Approximately $110M in annuity production assisted over six years, approximately $18M in
              current annual volume, and eight active producers. Insurance made Position and Shape obligations,
              not design language.
            </p>
            <div class="operator-evidence" aria-label="Insurance operating evidence">
              <div>
                <strong data-count-to="8">8</strong>
                <span>Active producers</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong data-count-to="18" data-count-prefix="~$" data-count-suffix="M">~$18M</strong>
                <span>Current annual annuity volume assisted</span>
              </div>
              <div>
                <strong data-count-to="110" data-count-prefix="~$" data-count-suffix="M">~$110M</strong>
                <span>Total annuity production assisted over six years</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <dl class="operator-facts">
              <div><dt>License</dt><dd>Texas Life, Health, and Annuity 3096607</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Specialty</dt><dd>FERS, CSRS, TSP, FEHB, and LEO, ATC, and researcher variations</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
          <div class="operator-station-transfer">
            <span>METHOD CONTRIBUTION</span>
            <strong>Position + Shape</strong>
            <p>Place responsibility where the person and the outcome can still be seen.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="operator-current" aria-labelledby="operator-current-title">
      <div class="operator-current-grid shell">
        <div class="operator-current-mark" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>NOW</span>
          <strong>01</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="operator-current-copy">
          <h2 id="operator-current-title">Still inside the business.</h2>
          <p>
            The method is not being developed from a distance. It is being tested against the business that already
            has to perform, with real producers, real cases, and real responsibility attached to the outcome.
          </p>
        </div>
        <blockquote class="operator-current-quote">Secure the foundation. Build the prospective state.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="operator-close" aria-labelledby="operator-close-title">
      <div class="operator-close-grid shell">
        <div class="operator-close-copy">
          <h2 id="operator-close-title">Secure the foundation.<br />Build the prospective state.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="operator-close-action">
          <p>Start with the work in front of you.</p>
          <a class="action action--signal" href="/contact">Start a direct conversation <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../scripts/motion.js';
  import '../scripts/pages/the-operator.js';
</script>
